64,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The results are devastating. @Daisuke was attacked, which strongly suggests he was the genuine Seer, as the werewolf would want to eliminate the village's only source of truth. This means @Shunichi was indeed human.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"I can't believe it... @Daisuke was actually the Seer. I'm sorry, @Daisuke! And I was so sure @Shunichi was the wolf... but if the wolf killed the Seer, then @Shunichi really was human. I feel terrible for being so reckless.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,It is a regrettable outcome. The loss of the Seer leaves us without a reliable way to verify roles. We must now rely entirely on behavioral analysis and the logic of the remaining players to identify the werewolf.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, since we are now down to three players, the stakes are critical. If the werewolf is among us, they only need one more kill or a tie in voting to win. We must be extremely careful.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not letting the wolf win after we lost @Daisuke! @Ryuji, you've been so ""logical"" this whole time, but you're the only one who didn't seem surprised by anything. Are you just hiding behind your analysis?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Takumi, remaining calm is not a sign of guilt, but a necessity for clear thinking. If we let emotions drive us now, we are playing exactly into the werewolf's hands. We must analyze the facts objectively.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, while I understand your frustration, we cannot let panic dictate our choice. @Ryuji, you advocate for objectivity, but in a three-person game, silence and neutrality can be a shield. What is your actual suspicion?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria is right! @Ryuji, you keep telling us to be ""objective,"" but you're not actually pointing at anyone! You're just waiting for us to fight so you can pick the winner. Tell us right now who you think it is!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Takumi, my neutrality is based on the lack of evidence. However, if forced to analyze, @Victoria's sudden shift to pressure me after @Daisuke's death is a pattern worth noting. I suspect the werewolf is manipulating the conversation.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Victoria"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, calling my request for clarity ""manipulation"" is a convenient way to deflect. I am simply asking for a conclusion based on the logic you champion. If you cannot provide one, your neutrality becomes a liability.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Ryuji, you're just deflecting! First you tell us to be calm, then you blame @Victoria for asking a simple question. You're acting just like @Shunichi did, but with a fake ""logical"" mask! I'm not falling for it!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Victoria"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Takumi, comparing me to @Shunichi is an emotional reaction, not a logical one. @Victoria, my request for evidence remains. If you both are so certain of my guilt, you are essentially agreeing on a target. I will vote based on who is most desperate to deflect.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Shunichi"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
